description:
The objectives of this Safety Sub-Registry are to collect uniform and meaningful data on patients with Pompe disease who experience anaphylaxis, severe allergic reactions, and/or signals of severe cutaneous and/or systemic immune-mediated reactions following treatment with alglucosidase alfa.  This Safety Sub-Registry also will assess:
•	the symptoms, severity, outcome, and occurrence of those adverse events (AEs; anaphylaxis, severe allergic reactions, and signals of severe cutaneous and systemic immune mediated reactions);
•	the effect of antibody responses (both timing and pattern of responses) and cross reacting immunologic material (CRIM) status (in patients with age at symptom onset less than or equal to 12 months only) on the occurrence of such AEs.

